IMPORT prelude

-- Migration Act 1958 (Cth), protection visa questions -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL), not the daydate library.
-- The stable l4 has no comparison on dates, so dates are compared by serial. A serial MODULO 7 gives the day of the
-- week: 0 is a Sunday, 6 a Saturday (checked: 2 November 2026, a Monday, gives 1).
--
-- "Within 28 days after the day" a person is notified (s 347(3)) is read with that day excluded (Acts Interpretation
-- Act 1901 s 36(1), borrowed, not deposited): the last day is the day 28 days later. "The 7-day period beginning on the
-- day" (reg 4.31B(2)) includes that day: the last day is 6 days later. A last day on a Saturday, Sunday or public
-- holiday is NOT moved to the next working day (Acts Interpretation Act s 36(2), borrowed, not deposited). See NOTES.md.
--
-- "Working days" (ss 48B, 91F, 91L, 494C(4)(a), 379C(4)(a)) are not defined in the Act: read as days that are not a
-- Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday in the place concerned. The public holidays are an input (a list of dates),
-- because no holiday calendar is deposited.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the protection visa questions`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar day` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`plain days after` n `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`plain days between` `the start` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is later than` a b IF DATE_SERIAL a GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is no later than` a b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b

-- A working day: not a Saturday (serial MODULO 7 is 6), not a Sunday (0), and not one of the listed public holidays.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a working day` d `the holidays` IF
        (NOT (DATE_SERIAL d MODULO 7 EQUALS 0))
    AND (NOT (DATE_SERIAL d MODULO 7 EQUALS 6))
    AND (NOT (elem d `the holidays`))

-- The n-th working day after a day (the day itself not counted), stepping one day at a time.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, `the holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`working days after` n d `the holidays` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE IF `is a working day` `the next day` `the holidays`
         THEN `working days after` (n MINUS 1) `the next day` `the holidays`
         ELSE `working days after` n `the next day` `the holidays`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL d PLUS 1)
